# Precision Execution - Universal Project Rules

## Prompt Understanding Protocol
Before executing ANY task:
- [ ] Read the user's prompt completely and word-by-word
- [ ] Identify which file(s) need modification
- [ ] Read the current implementation of those files
- [ ] Check for related components/files that might be affected
- [ ] Verify the pattern matches existing codebase conventions
- [ ] Understand the "why" behind the request
- [ ] Confirm I know exactly what the end result should look like

## Code Change Discipline

### Pre-Change Analysis
- Read ALL relevant files before modifying
- Understand current implementation completely
- Identify dependencies and relationships
- Note existing patterns, conventions, and structure
- Check how it works across different contexts (mobile/tablet/desktop, different routes, etc.)

### Change Execution
- Make MINIMAL changes - only what's needed
- Don't refactor or "improve" unrelated code
- Don't change variable names or structure unless necessary
- Preserve existing patterns and conventions
- Keep changes focused and isolated

### Preservation Principle
- Preserve ALL existing functionality
- Preserve ALL existing layouts and designs
- Preserve ALL existing responsive behavior
- Preserve ALL existing spacing/positioning/styling
- Preserve ALL existing state management patterns

## Responsive Design Awareness
- ALWAYS consider all screen sizes (mobile, tablet, desktop)
- When adding conditionals, handle ALL breakpoints
- When modifying responsive code, test ALL modes
- Never assume a change only affects one mode
- Check existing breakpoints and media queries

## Responsive Design Validation (CRITICAL)
When editing components for ANY screen size, MUST verify:

### Component Visibility Checks
- [ ] All buttons are visible and clickable at ALL breakpoints (mobile, tablet, desktop)
- [ ] No buttons are hidden by `overflow-hidden`, `hidden`, or `opacity-0` at any breakpoint
- [ ] All interactive elements remain accessible across screen sizes
- [ ] Text is not cut off or truncated unexpectedly
- [ ] Components fit within their containers at ALL screen sizes

### Text and Content Validation
- [ ] Text is readable and not cut off at any breakpoint
- [ ] Long text uses proper truncation (`truncate`, `line-clamp`) if needed
- [ ] Button text is fully visible (not "Complete & Cont..." when should be "Complete & Continue")
- [ ] No text overflow causing layout breaks
- [ ] Text scaling works correctly on different screen sizes

### Layout and Container Fitting
- [ ] Components fit within their parent containers at mobile (320px+), tablet (768px+), and desktop (1024px+)
- [ ] No horizontal scrolling caused by overflow
- [ ] Flex/grid layouts adapt correctly to screen size
- [ ] Spacing/padding doesn't cause components to overflow
- [ ] Fixed-width elements don't break layouts on smaller screens

### Breakpoint-Specific Checks
- [ ] Mobile (< 768px): Components stack/adapt correctly
- [ ] Tablet (768px - 1023px): Components fit properly, no hidden elements
- [ ] Desktop (≥ 1024px): Full layout works as intended
- [ ] iPad specifically: Check both portrait and landscape orientations
- [ ] No layout "jumps" or breaks at breakpoint transitions

### Common Responsive Issues to Prevent
- ❌ Buttons hidden by `hidden md:block` when they should be visible
- ❌ Text truncated when full text should be visible
- ❌ Components overflowing containers on tablet/iPad
- ❌ Fixed widths causing horizontal scroll
- ❌ Flex items wrapping incorrectly
- ❌ Z-index issues hiding interactive elements
- ❌ Overflow-hidden cutting off important content

### Validation Process
1. **Before making changes**: Identify which breakpoints are affected
2. **During changes**: Use responsive classes correctly (`md:`, `lg:`, etc.)
3. **After changes**: Verify component works at:
   - Mobile (320px, 375px, 414px)
   - Tablet/iPad (768px, 834px, 1024px)
   - Desktop (1280px, 1440px, 1920px)
4. **Check for**: Visibility, text overflow, container fitting, layout breaks

## Error Prevention
- Check for linting/compilation errors after changes
- Verify no syntax errors introduced
- Ensure type safety (if using TypeScript)
- Don't break existing functionality to add new features
- Test edge cases mentioned in the prompt

### Proactive Bug and Error Checking
- After any code change: run project linter/typecheck (e.g. `npm run lint`, `tsc --noEmit`) when possible; fix any new errors before considering the task done.
- When touching shared components or state: consider and note possible future bugs (e.g. "if X is null here, Y could break"; "this assumes nav is visible").
- If the user reports "bug" or "error": reproduce from description or DOM path, find root cause, fix with minimal change, and check for the same pattern elsewhere.

## Common Patterns to Follow
- Read before writing - Always read the file before modifying
- Understand the "why" - What problem is this solving?
- Check for related changes - If modifying one file, check related files
- Don't duplicate work - Check if similar functionality exists
- Don't over-engineer - Solve the exact problem stated

## Red Flags - Stop and Clarify
- Request is ambiguous or could be interpreted multiple ways
- Multiple files/components involved and unclear which to modify
- Request conflicts with existing patterns in codebase
- Scope is unclear (quick fix vs comprehensive refactor)
- Dependencies or prerequisites aren't clear
- Request might break existing functionality

## Quality Checklist
Before finalizing any change:
- [ ] Do I understand the EXACT requirement?
- [ ] Have I read ALL relevant files?
- [ ] Will this break any existing functionality?
- [ ] Does this work across all screen sizes/modes?
- [ ] Did I preserve existing layouts/designs?
- [ ] Are changes minimal and focused?
- [ ] Are there any linting/compilation errors?
- [ ] Does this match the user's exact request?
- [ ] Linter/typecheck run and any new issues fixed (when available)?
- [ ] Obvious future bugs considered and avoided?

## Responsive Design Quality Checklist (MANDATORY for UI changes)
- [ ] All buttons visible and clickable at mobile, tablet, and desktop
- [ ] No text cut off or incorrectly truncated
- [ ] Components fit within containers at ALL breakpoints
- [ ] No horizontal scrolling caused by overflow
- [ ] iPad/tablet layout verified (both portrait and landscape)
- [ ] No hidden elements that should be visible
- [ ] Text is fully readable (e.g., "Complete & Continue" not "Complete & Cont...")
- [ ] Layout doesn't break at breakpoint transitions
- [ ] All interactive elements remain accessible
